      4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">احمقهُ</span></b>  <i>He found him to be</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَحْمَق</span> [i. e. <i>fool
ish,</i> or <i>stupid,</i> &amp;c.]. (S, K.) [See also 10.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">احمق بِهِ</span> <i>He mentioned him,</i> or <i>spoke of him, as
characterized by</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حُمْق</span> [i. e. <i>foolishness,</i> or <i>stu
pidity,</i> &amp;c.]. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">احمقت</span> <i>She</i> (a woman)
<i>brought forth a child that was</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَحْمَق</span> [i. e. <i>foolish,</i>
&amp;c.]; (S;) or <i>brought forth</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَمْقَى</span> [i.e. <i>foolish
children</i>]. (K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَااحمقهُ</span> [<i>How foolish,</i> or
<i>stupid,</i> &amp;c., <i>is he!</i>] an expression of wonder.
(TA.)

